This repository is released under two licences, because it holds two kinds of
thing and they carry different obligations. `CITATION_AND_LICENCE.md` records
the audit this follows from, traced from import statements and data files
rather than assumed.

    pipeline/                     MIT
    verification/, figures/       CC BY 4.0
    MANIFEST.json, PATH_MAP.json,
    README.md, this file          CC BY 4.0

Nothing copyleft is linked into the code. GROMACS, AmberTools, Open Babel and
pdb2pqr are invoked as separate executables through subprocess and never
imported, so no copyleft term propagates. Every in-process import is
BSD-3-Clause, MIT or Apache-2.0 -- including Meeko 0.3.3, confirmed Apache-2.0
from the installed distribution's own metadata on 2026-09-13.

**Attribution required for the data.** Files under `verification/` carry
structures, InChIKeys and organism names derived from LOTUS v11
(doi:10.5281/zenodo.19360665), which is CC BY 4.0. LOTUS must be credited
wherever those files are reused.

**A note for anyone extending this.** ChEMBL is CC BY-SA 3.0 and is share-alike.
No ChEMBL records are deposited here -- only aggregate statistics from models
trained on them -- so share-alike is not triggered. If the frozen ChEMBL extract
is ever added, that portion must be released under CC BY-SA 3.0 and not under
CC BY 4.0.

